Description: Accelerated array computing and code transformations for R.
    Numerical programs operating on multi-dimensional arrays can be
    just-in-time compiled to optimized executables via 'XLA' -- the same
    compiler that powers 'JAX' and 'TensorFlow' -- and run on CPU or
    NVIDIA GPU from the same source. Also provides reverse-mode automatic
    differentiation, returning the gradient of a function as another R
    function.
